 user\'s main goal is to find the root cause of any faults. The initial problem might be that the `reservation` service isn\'t functioning because it has no endpoints, which could be due to the pod not being properly assigned. So the next step is to check the pod\'s details to see why it\'s not being discovered by the service. \n\nTherefore, the user should run `kubectl describe pod reservation-0 -n hotel-reservation` to check for any issues with the pod, such as readiness probes failing, or the container not starting correctly. If the pod is crashing, that\'s the root cause. Alternatively, if the pod is running but not labeled correctly, that\'s the issue. \n\nSo the next tool call should be to describe the pod to get more details on its status and any potential errors.\n</think>\n\ntool name: exec_read_only_kubectl_cmd  \nreasoning: The `reservation` service has no endpoints despite the pod being listed as running. This suggests a mismatch between the pod\'s labels and the service\'s selector, or the pod is not properly assigned. Describing the pod will reveal its status, readiness, and any errors preventing it from being discovered by the service.  \n\ntool_call: {  \n  "command": "kubectl describe pod reservation-0 -n hotel-reservation"  \n}', additional_kwargs={'provider_specific_fields': {'reasoning': None, 'refusal': None}}, response_metadata={'token_usage': {'completion_tokens': 1460, 'prompt_tokens': 8516, 'total_tokens': 9976, 'completion_tokens_details': None, 'prompt_tokens_details': None}, 'model': 'openai/Qwen/Qwen3-8B', 'finish_reason': 'stop', 'logprobs': None, 'model_name': 'openai/Qwen/Qwen3-8B'}, id='lc_run--019cfe3e-ba77-7d12-9696-c4586bb7e010-0', tool_calls=[], invalid_tool_calls=[], usage_metadata={'input_tokens': 8516, 'output_tokens': 1460, 'total_tokens': 9976}), HumanMessage(content='Now generate a tool call according to your last chosen tool.', additional_kwargs={}, response_metadata={}, id='4177642f-d29e-46af-bfc2-558dab6bfadc'), AIMessag