 the endpoints are still empty. This could be because the pods aren\'t labeled correctly or there\'s a mismatch between the service selector and the pod labels.\n\nLooking at the deployment\'s pod template, the labels include \'io.kompose.service=reservation\', which matches the service\'s selector. So the labels seem correct. However, maybe the pods aren\'t being properly registered with the service. Another possibility is that the service is not correctly configured to expose the metrics port, which might be related to the missing HTTP requests metrics.\n\nThe user also tried checking the logs for the pod \'reservation-0\' but got a \'Not Found\' error. Now that they know the correct pod name is \'reservation-7bb77b596b-8zbb6\', they should check the logs for that pod to see if there are any errors or issues preventing the service from functioning properly. \n\nAdditionally, since the metrics for HTTP requests aren\'t showing up, it\'s possible that the Prometheus exporter isn\'t configured correctly for the \'reservation\' service. They should check if the service is exposing the metrics endpoint (like /metrics) on the correct port and if Prometheus is scraping those metrics. \n\nAnother angle is to check the network policies or firewall rules to ensure that traffic can reach the service. But given the previous steps, the main suspects are the service configuration, pod labels, and metrics exposure. The next logical step is to check the logs of the \'reservation\' pod to see if there are any runtime errors or issues that might be causing the service to not register endpoints or expose metrics properly.\n</think>\n\ntool name: exec_read_only_kubectl_cmd  \nreasoning: The pod `reservation-0` no longer exists; the correct pod name is `reservation-7bb77b596b-8zbb6`. To debug why the service has no endpoints, I need to check the logs of the `reservation` pod for runtime errors, failed container startups, or misconfigurations that prevent it from being discovered by the service.  \n\ntool_call: {  \n  "command": "kubectl logs -n hotel-reservation reservation-7bb77b596b-8zbb6"  \n}', additional_kwargs={'provider_specific_fields': {'reasoning': None, 'refusal': None}}, response_metadata={'token_usage': {'completion_tokens': 688, 'prompt_tokens': 9663, 'total_tokens': 10351, 'completion_tokens_details': None, 'prompt_tokens_details': None}, 'model': 'openai/Qwen/Qwen3-8B', 'finish_reason': 'stop', 'logprobs': None, 'model_name': 'openai/Qwen/Qwen3-8B'}, id='lc_run--019cfe3f-8508-74d3-bf97-55ec1e992c31-0', tool_calls=[], invalid_tool_calls=[], usage_metadata={'input_tokens': 9663, 'output_tokens': 688, 'total_tokens': 10351}), HumanMessage(content='Now generate a tool call according to your last chosen tool.', additional_kwargs={}, response_metadata={}, id='f13b20a6-73b8-4203-8141-6bbc5587c319'), AIMessage(content="<think>\nOkay, let's see. The user is trying to diagnose an issue with the Hotel Reservation application. They've been checking various components like deployments, services, and pods. The main problem seems to be that the 'reservation' service isn't showing any endpoints, which means the pods aren't being discovered by the service. \n\nFirst, they checked the deployments and found that the reservation deployment is running with one pod, reservation-7bb77b596b-8zbb6. The service 'reservation' is configured to target port 8087, but the endpoints are empty. That suggests a mismatch between the service's selector and the pod's labels.\n\nWait, the service's selector is 'io.kompose.service=reservation', and the pod's labels include that same key. So why no endpoints? Maybe the pod isn't actually running or there's a problem with the container. The user tried to get the pod's logs but got an error because they used the wrong pod name. Now they're using the correct pod name, reservation-7bb77b596b-8zbb6.\n\nLooking at the logs might show if the container is crashing or there are errors during startup. If the logs indicate a problem, like a failed application startup or missing dependencies, that could explain why the service isn't getting endpoints. Also, checking the pod's status and events could reveal if there are any restarts or errors. \n\nAnother angle: maybe the service isn't configured to expose the correct port for metrics, which is why the Prometheus query for http_requests_total didn't return any data. But the user's main issue now is the missing endpoints for the reservation service. \n\nSo, the next step is to check the logs of the reservation pod to see if there are any errors or issues that prevent it from being discovered by the service. If the logs are clear, maybe the problem is with the service configuration or network policies. But since the service is ClusterIP and the pod is running, the logs are the next best clue.\n</think>\n\n", additional_kwargs={'tool_calls': [{'function': {'arguments': '{"command": "kubectl logs -n hotel-reservation reservation-7bb77b596b-8zbb6"}', 'name': 'exec_read_only_kubectl_cmd'}, 'id': 'chatcmpl-tool-82523048abeea51d', 'type': 'function'}], 'provider_specific_fields': {'reasoning': None, 'refusal': None}}, response_metadata={'token_usage': {'completion_tokens': 469, 'prompt_tokens': 10695, 'total_tokens': 11164, 'completion_tokens_details': None, 'prompt_tokens_details': None}, 'model': 'openai/Qwen/Qwen3-8B', 'finish_reason': 'tool_calls', 'logprobs': None, 'model_name': 'openai/Qwen/Qwen3-8B'}, id='lc_run--019cfe3f-a728-75d3-afc0-5d0a386ce253-0', tool_calls=[{'name': 'exec_read_only_kubectl_cmd', 'args': {'command': 'kubectl logs -n hotel-reservation reservation-7bb77b596b-8zbb6'}, 'id': 'chatcmpl-tool-82523048abeea51d', 'type': 'tool_call'}], invalid_tool_calls=[], usage_metadata={'input_tokens': 10695, 'output_tokens': 469, 'total_tokens': 11164}), ToolMessage(content='{"level":"info","time":"2026-03-17T23:58:48Z","message":"TLS disabled."}\n{"level":"info","time":"2026-03-17T23:58:48Z","message":"Set global log level: info"}\n{"level":"info","time":"2026-03-17T23:58:48Z","message":"Tune: setGCPercent to 100"}\n\x1b[90m2026-03-17T23:58:48Z\x1b[0m \x1b[32mINF\x1b[0m \x1b[1mcmd/reservation/main.go:25\x1b[0m\x1b[36m >\x1b[0m \x1b[1mReading config...\x1b[0m\n\x1b[90m2026-03-17T23:58:48Z\x1b[0m \x1b[32mINF\x1b[0m \x1b[1mcmd/reservation/main.go:38\x1b[0m\x1b[36m >\x1b[0m \x1b[1mRead database URL: mongodb-reservation:27017\x1b[0m\n\x1b[90m2026-03-17T23:58:48Z\x1b[0m \x1b[32mINF\x1b[0m \x1b[1mcmd/reservation/main.go:39\x1b[0m\x1b[36m >\x1b[0m \x1b[1mInitializing DB connection...\x1b[0m\n\x1b[90m2026-03-17T23:58:48Z\x1b[0m \x1b[32mINF\x1b[0m \x1b[1mcmd/reservation/db.go:30\x1b[0m\x1b[36m >\x1b[0m \x1b[1mNew session successfull...\x1b[0m\n\x1b[90m2026-03-17T23:58:49Z\x1b[0m \x1b[32mINF\x1b[0m \x1b[1mcmd/reservation/main.go:42\x1b[0m\x1b[36m >\x1b[0m \x1b[1mSuccessfull\x1b[0m\n\x1b[90m2026-03-17T23:58:49Z\x1b[0m \x1b[32mINF\x1b[0m \x1b[1mcmd/reservation/main.go:44\x1b[0m\x1b[36m >\x1b[0m \x1b[1mRead profile memcashed address: memcached-reserve:11211\x1b[0m\n\x1b[90m2026-03-17T23:58:49Z\x1b[0m \x1b[32mINF\x1b[0m \x1b[1mcmd/reservation/main.go:45\x1b[0m\x1b[36m >\x1b[0m \x1b[1mInitializing Memcashed client...\x1b[0m\n\x1b[90m2026-03-17T23:58:49Z\x1b[0m \x1b[32mINF\x1b[0m \x1b[1mtune/setting.go:61\x1b[0m\x1b[36m >\x1b[0m \x1b[1mTune: GetMemCTimeout 2\x1b[0m\n\x1b[90m2026-03-17T23:58:49Z\x1b[0m \x1b[32mINF\x1b[0m \x1b[1mcmd/reservation/main.go:47\x1b[0m\x1b[36m >\x1b[0m \x1b[1mSuccessfull\x1b[0m\n\x1b[90m2026-03-17T23:58:49Z\x1b[0m \x1b[32mINF\x1b[0m \x1b[1mcmd/reservation/main.go:51\x1b[0m\x1b[36m >\x1b[0m \x1b[1mRead target port: 8087\x1b[0m\n\x1b[90m2026-03-17T23:58:49Z\x1b[0m \x1b[32mINF\x1b[0m \x1b[1mcmd/reservation/main.go:52\x1b[0m\x1b[36m >\x1b[0m \x1b[1mRead consul address: consul:8500\x1b[0m\n\x1b[90m2026-03-17T23:58:49Z\x1b[0m \x1b[32mINF\x1b[0m \x1b[1mcmd/reservation/main.go:53\x1b[0m\x1b[36m >\x1b[0m \x1b[1mRead jaeger address: jaeger:6831\x1b[0m\n\x1b[90m2026-03-17T23:58:49Z\x1b[0m \x1b[32mINF\x1